# Jira register (live-read 2026-08-21)

- Cloud: `https://eliteintegrityservices.atlassian.net` — project **P2024** (Elite Integrity - Engineering)
- REST v3 with operator email + API token. **Never store tokens in this folder.**
- Types: **Project** (job) → **Task** (package) → **Sub-task** (drawing). Dummy job `P2024-15553` spawned this template.

## Pack list = every issue with this Job Number

- Search: `project = P2024 AND issuetype != Project AND "Job Number" ~ "{job}"` (Tasks, Sub-tasks, EDDI items — not only `labels = Drafting`).
- Also walk the job **Project** issue for that Job Number: direct children and their sub-tasks, even when Job Number was never copied onto those issues.
- After Load, show that **Project** issue’s summary and key (dummy `P2024-15553`) next to the matched or Located Dropbox job folder. Several Job Numbers may share one folder; they stay two Loads / two register lists.
- Group on the console by EDDI Status (1–9), header row between groups. Blank EDDI → Ungrouped. **0 Generic is not listed.**
- Missing PDF: **Locate…** on the row (pairs the file; does not rewrite Jira). **Locate…** stays after a match so the operator can pick a different file. **Paste PDF** (Outlook Copy, then the navy button or Ctrl+V) is the ingest — there is no PDF from Outlook hunt button. A paste pair shows the PDF **filename** followed by **— email dropped** (yellow) instead of the Dropbox path, so the operator can confirm which file paired; hover gives the full wording and the staged path. Several Outlook attachments Copied at once wait in **New PDFs** for Assign. Locate… of a real job PDF clears the yellow, leaves the plain filename, and deletes our `DocCon/dropped` copy (not the Locate’d file). **Rename…** is only for an email-dropped copy (the zip name); a Locate’d Dropbox PDF is never renamed. **Open** beside it opens the paired PDF in the Windows default reader (disabled until a file is paired; missing file is a short error). The file picker opens in the matched Dropbox job folder on Load, then remembers the last pick until the next Load (LOCALAPPDATA, not Dropbox).
- Drawings are still Sub-tasks under the Drawing Package (label `Drafting`). Dummy drawings: `P2024-15578` `2026-Tanzim-1-1 Drawing-1`, `P2024-15579` `2026-Tanzim-1-2 Drawing-2`
- Live summary shape: ID is the leading code (`2026-075-1-STWD`, `2026-075-ITP-1-1`); wording after that is the description. Empty description is fine. Job Number field is the grouping key.
- **JIRA ID and Description are both editable Next fields** (1.55) and both map to `summary`. Confirm composes one `summary` per issue from the effective ID + effective description (single space, no trailing space). Preflight rejects only a blank or internal-whitespace ID Next. An ID edit never re-pairs or drops a PDF (pairing is keyed by issue key).
- **Create Sub-task from the console** (1.69): compact **Create new Jira Issue** on the navy identity row. Operator picks Parent (Tasks under the loaded job Project), EDDI Status 1–9, JIRA ID, Description. Job Number and Project Lead / Sponsor copy from that Project. Immediate `POST /issue`. Meter: Creating on Jira… → Created → Fetching from Jira…; GET-by-key merge if search lags. Do not create a Task or Project from this flow.

## Field map

| Use | Field | ID |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Job | Job Number | `customfield_10300` (on create: copy from the job Project/epic, not typed) |
| Project Lead / Sponsor | Project Lead / Sponsor | `customfield_10071` (People; required on the Project/epic, not on Sub-task create. On create: copy account ids from the epic; omit if empty. Not the Jira software lead for `P2024`.) |
| Due date | Due date | `duedate` (not edited on the console; Confirm writes it from Return Request Date when that Next date is entered) |
| Client Doc No. | Client Document Number | `customfield_10279` (text) |
| Outgoing revision | Outgoing Rev | `customfield_10280` |
| Submitted to Client For | Submitted to Client For | `customfield_10281` (Approval / Info / Planned / Construction / NA) |
| Submitted to Shop For | Submitted to Shop For | `customfield_10626` (IFC / IFI / IFU / Purchasing Only) |
| Submitted to Field For | Submitted to Field For | `customfield_10625` (IFC / IFI) |
| Submission Date | Submission Date | `customfield_10301` |
| Return Request Date | Return Request Date | `customfield_10046` |
| Incoming rev | Incoming Rev | `customfield_10283` |
| Client Approval Status | Client Approval Status | `customfield_10284` (Approved / Approved with Comments / Revise & Resubmit / Rejected / Info / Void) |
| Return Date | Return Date | `customfield_10066` |
| Shop Rev / Shop Issue Date | Shop Rev / Shop Issue Date | `customfield_10285` / `customfield_10286` |
| Field Rev / Field Issue Date | Field Rev / Field Issue Date | `customfield_10287` / `customfield_10288` |
| EDDI Status | EDDI Status | `customfield_10289` (multi-checkbox; DocCon needs one option). On Load, more than one value prompts for a single 1–9 choice, writes that, and reloads. Skip continues Load with the messy multi-status. Generic (0) is not listed on the board. Options come from **that issue's own** `editmeta` `allowedValues` (one GET per Jira issue type; multi-checkbox contexts are per project / issue type) and are written **by option id**. Option labels are separated by `;` only — group 5 (`5 - QC - WO, ITP, NDE Records, Procedures - EDDI`) has commas inside its name. A label not on that issue's context aborts in the Confirm preflight; nothing is written (1.54). |

All of those (plus workflow **Status**) except **Due Date** are Now/Next on the pack board. Confirm writes filled Next values, and writes Jira Due Date from a newly entered Return Request Date. Cover Date issued / Expected return stay on the Excel letter (not Jira fields by themselves). Load starts **Date issued** at today and **Expected return** at N/A with Pack off and **Set packed to** blank. Expected return stamps packed Next Return Request Date (`customfield_10046`) to the same calendar day; Confirm writes that to Jira and copies a newly entered value to `duedate`. Cover Date issued stamps packed Next Submission Date (`customfield_10301`) the same way. **Set packed to** (Jira Status: OFA, IFI, …) stamps packed Next Status the same way. Setting a cover date back to N/A restores that packed Next date to Now; blank Set packed to restores packed Status to Now. Pack-tick with blank/N/A does not wipe a typed Next. Blank Expected return → N/A on the letter. Blank/N/A Date issued → today on the letter. Expected return presets: Urgent same day, Urgent +1, 7 days, 14 days (calendar days from Date issued). Cancel Next restores Date issued to today and Expected return to N/A. Submitted to Client For, Submitted to Shop For, Submitted to Field For, Client Approval Status, Shop Rev, Field Rev, and EDDI Status are pick-only lists (same as Status).

Sub-task statuses: To Do, In Progress, OFA, Awaiting Client Information, Roadblock, Back from Client, IFI, IFC, Done.

Template also has Task `Document Transmittals` (label `DocCon`) — a work package, not the drawing register.

Log numbering (locked 2026-09-01): `CT|ST|FT-{Job Number}-{n}` from the job Excel books under `3.0 Doc Con`. Client STATUS list: APPROVAL, CONSTRUCTION, INFORMATION, REVIEW, AS-BUILT (not the same labels as Jira purpose).

Controllers today edit those fields in a Jira Excel export. That file is not a second register. They will edit the same fields **on the DocCon console**; confirm writes Jira REST on the drawing sub-task.

